#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:12
msgid "Fluid Deformation and Energy Dissipation Derivations"
msgstr "Derivaciones de deformación de fluidos y disipación de energía"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:17
msgid "Equations for :math:`\\varepsilon` and :math:`G` in Varying Flow Geometries"
msgstr ""
"Ecuaciones para :math:`\\varepsilon` y :math:`G` en Geometrías de Flujo "
"Variables"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:19
msgid ""
"Estimation of velocity gradients for various flow geometries is the basis "
"for the design of rapid mix, flocculators, and plate settlers. Thus, our "
"goal is to define the velocity gradients consistently across a range of "
"possible flow regimes. There are three approaches to calculating the average"
" velocity gradient within a control volume."
msgstr ""
"La estimación de gradientes de velocidad para diversas geometrías de flujo "
"es la base para el diseño de mezcla rápida, floculadores y sedimentadores de"
" placas. Por tanto, nuestro objetivo es definir los gradientes de velocidad "
"de forma consistente a lo largo de una gama de posibles regímenes de flujo. "
"Existen tres enfoques para calcular el gradiente medio de velocidad dentro "
"de un volumen de control."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:21
msgid ""
"Use the Navier Stokes equations and solve for the spatially averaged "
"velocity gradient."
msgstr ""
"Utiliza las ecuaciones de Navier Stokes y resuelve el gradiente de velocidad"
" promediado espacialmente."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:22
msgid ""
"Use Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) to solve for the spatially averaged "
"velocity gradient."
msgstr ""
"Utiliza la Dinámica de Fluidos Computacional (CFD) para resolver el "
"gradiente de velocidad promediado espacialmente."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:23
msgid ""
"Use the total mechanical energy loss in the control volume to calculate the "
"energy dissipation rate. Estimate the velocity gradient directly from the "
"energy dissipation rate, :math:`\\tilde{G} = "
"\\sqrt{\\frac{\\bar\\varepsilon}{\\nu}}`, as defined by Camp and Stein in "
"1943 (Camp, T. R., and Stein, P. C. (1943) ‘‘Velocity Gradients and "
"Hydraulic Work in Fluid Motion,’’ J. Boston Soc. Civil Eng., 30, 203–221.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:25
msgid ""
"The first approach would be ideal but is difficult in practice because "
"Navier Stokes solutions are only available for limited geometries and "
"laminar flow. CFD could be used but is difficult to use as a general "
"engineering design approach given the large number of geometries that are "
"used in drinking water treatment plants. For these reasons we will use the "
"control volume approach to estimate the average velocity gradient. This "
"method incorrectly assumes that the energy dissipation rate is completely "
"uniform in the control volume and hence the velocity gradient is also "
"uniform. This method results in an over estimation of the velocity gradient."
" The Camp-Stein estimate of :math:`\\tilde{G}` is based on a control volume "
"where the velocity gradient is uniform. Consider a layer of fluid of depth "
":math:`H` and apply a velocity, :math:`v` at the top of the fluid. The "
"velocity gradient, :math:`G`, is thus :math:`\\frac{v}{H}` everywhere in the"
" fluid. The force required to move the top of the fluid at velocity v can be"
" obtained from the required shear, :math:`\\tau`. From Newtons Law of "
"Friction we have"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:28
msgid "\\tau = \\mu \\frac{v}{H} = \\mu G = \\nu\\rho G"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:33
msgid "Where :math:`\\tau` is the force required per unit plan view area."
msgstr ""
"Donde :math:`\\tau` es la fuerza requerida por unidad de área de vista en "
"planta."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:35
msgid ""
"Figure :numref:`figure_G_velocity_profile` shows the velocity profile of a "
"fluid deforming under the influence of uniform shear."
msgstr ""
"La figura :numref:`figure_G_velocity_profile` muestra el perfil de velocidad"
" de un fluido que se deforma bajo la influencia de cizalladura uniforme."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:44
msgid "fluid deformation"
msgstr "Deformación del fluido"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:44
msgid "The velocity profile of a fluid being deformed by uniform shear."
msgstr "El perfil de velocidad de un fluido deformado por cizalladura uniforme."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:48
msgid ""
":math:`G` measures the magnitude of shear by using the velocity gradient of "
"a fluid in space, :math:`\\frac{\\Delta \\bar v}{\\Delta h}`. This is "
"essentially the same as the :math:`\\frac{\\delta u}{\\delta y}` term in "
"fluid mechanics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:50
msgid ""
"The power per unit area required to move the fluid at velocity :math:`v` is "
":math:`\\tau v`. The mass per unit area is :math:`\\rho H`. Thus the energy "
"dissipation rate or the power per mass is"
msgstr ""
"La potencia por unidad de área necesaria para mover el fluido a velocidad "
":math:`v` es :math:`\\tau v`. La masa por unidad de área es :math:`\\rho H`."
" Así, la tasa de disipación de energía o la potencia por masa es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:52
msgid ""
"\\varepsilon = \\frac{P}{m} = \\frac{\\tau v}{\\rho H} = \\frac{\\nu \\rho G"
" v}{\\rho H} = \\nu G^2\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:54
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\varepsilon`, which represents the **energy dissipation** rate"
" of a fluid *normalized by its mass*. The units of :math:`\\varepsilon` are "
"Watts per kilogram:"
msgstr ""
"donde :math:`\\varepsilon`, que representa la tasa de **disipación de "
"energía** de un fluido *normalizada por su masa*. Las unidades de "
":math:`\\varepsilon` son vatios por kilogramo:"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:56
msgid ""
"\\varepsilon = \\left[ \\frac{W}{Kg} \\right] = \\left[ \\frac{J}{s \\cdot "
"Kg} \\right] = \\left[ \\frac{N \\cdot m}{s \\cdot Kg} \\right] = \\left[ "
"\\frac{kg \\cdot m \\cdot m}{s^2 \\cdot s \\cdot Kg} \\right] = \\left[ "
"\\frac{m^2}{s^3} \\right] = \\left[ \\frac{[L]^2}{[T]^3} \\right]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:60
#, python-format
msgid ""
"There are at least two ways to think about :math:`\\varepsilon`. One is "
"through :math:`G`. Imagine that a fluid has *no viscosity*; there is no "
"internal friction caused by fluid flow. No matter how high :math:`G` "
"becomes, no energy is dissipated. Now image honey, which has a very high "
"viscosity. Making honey flow fast requires a lot of energy over a short "
"period of time, which means a high energy dissipation rate. This explanation"
" allows us to understand the equation for :math:`\\varepsilon` in terms of "
":math:`G` and :math:`\\nu`. `See this textbook "
"<https://app.knovel.com/web/view/khtml/show.v/rcid:kpMWHWTPD1/cid:kt00AD4KW1/viewerType:khtml/root_slug:mwh-s"
"-water-treatment/url_slug:principles-reactor-analysis?&b-toc-"
"cid=kpMWHWTPD1&b-toc-url-slug=coagulation-flocculation&b-toc-"
"title=MWH%E2%80%99s%20Water%20Treatment%20-%20Principles%20and%20Design%20(3rd%20Edition)&page=80&view=collapsed&zoom=1)>`_"
" for the derivation of the following equation:"
msgstr ""
"Hay al menos dos formas de pensar en :math:`\\varepsilon`. Una es a través "
"de :math:`G`. Imagina que un fluido tiene *no viscosity*; no hay fricción "
"interna causada por el flujo del fluido. Por muy alta que llegue :math:`G`, "
"no se disipa energía. Ahora imagina la miel, que tiene una viscosidad muy "
"alta. Hacer que la miel fluya rápido requiere mucha energía en un corto "
"periodo de tiempo, lo que implica una alta tasa de disipación de energía. "
"Esta explicación nos permite entender la ecuación para :math:`\\varepsilon` "
"en términos de :math:`G` y :math:`\\nu`. `See this textbook "
"<https://app.knovel.com/web/view/khtml/show.v/rcid:kpMWHWTPD1/cid:kt00AD4KW1/viewerType:khtml/root_slug:mwh-s"
"-water-treatment/url_slug:principles-reactor-analysis?&b-toc-"
"cid=kpMWHWTPD1&b-toc-url-slug=coagulation-flocculation&b-toc-"
"title=MWH%E2%80%99s%20Water%20Treatment%20-%20Principles%20and%20Design%20(3rd%20Edition)&page=80&view=collapsed&zoom=1)>`_"
" para la derivación de la siguiente ecuación:"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:62
msgid " \\varepsilon = \\nu G^2"
msgstr " \\varepsilon = \\nu G^2"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:67
msgid ""
"This equation has no approximations, but has one very important assumption. "
"We derived this equation for a control volume where the velocity gradient "
"was **uniform**. The reactors and control volumes that we will be using as "
"we design water treatment plants will **not** have uniform velocity "
"gradients. Indeed, several of the water treatment processes will be "
"turbulent and thus the velocity gradients in the fluid will vary in both "
"space and time. Even in laminar flow in a pipe the velocity gradient is far "
"from uniform with high velocity gradients at the wall and zero velocity "
"gradient at the center of the pipe."
msgstr ""
"Esta ecuación no tiene aproximaciones, pero tiene una suposición muy "
"importante. Derivamos esta ecuación para un volumen de control donde el "
"gradiente de velocidad era **uniforme**. Los reactores y volúmenes de "
"control que utilizaremos al diseñar tratamiento de agua plantas **no** "
"tendrán gradientes de velocidad uniformes. De hecho, varios de los procesos "
"tratamiento de agua serán turbulentos y, por tanto, los gradientes de "
"velocidad en el fluido variarán tanto en espacio como en tiempo. Incluso en "
"el flujo laminar en una tubería, el gradiente de velocidad dista mucho de "
"ser uniforme, con altos gradientes de velocidad en la pared y gradiente de "
"velocidad cero en el centro de la tubería."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:69
msgid ""
"We’d like to know if we can apply Equation :eq:`EDRofG_nu` to the case where"
" the energy dissipation rate and velocity gradients are nonuniform by simply"
" introducing average values of both quantities."
msgstr ""
"Nos gustaría saber si podemos aplicar la Ecuación :eq:`EDRofG_nu` al caso en"
" que la tasa de disipación de energía y los gradientes de velocidad no sean "
"uniformes simplemente introduciendo valores medios de ambas magnitudes."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:71
msgid ""
"\\bar\\varepsilon \\overset{?}{=} \\nu \\bar G^2\n"
"\n"
msgstr "\\bar\\varepsilon \\overset{?} {=} \\nu \\bar G^2"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:73
msgid ""
"We will test this option with a simple case. Consider a hypothetical reactor"
" (case 2) that is 4 times as large in plan view area as the uniform velocity"
" gradient case explored above (case 1). In addition, assume that 3/4 of the "
"reactor has a velocity gradient of zero. The average energy dissipation rate"
" for case 1 is"
msgstr ""
"Probaremos esta opción con un caso sencillo. Consideremos un reactor "
"hipotético (caso 2) que es 4 veces más grande en el área de vista en planta "
"que el caso de gradiente de velocidad uniforme explorado anteriormente (caso"
" 1). Además, supongamos que 3/4 del reactor tiene un gradiente de velocidad "
"cero. La tasa media de disipación de energía para el caso 1 es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:75
msgid ""
"\\bar \\varepsilon_1 = \\frac{P_1}{m_1} =  \\nu \\bar G_1^2\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:77
msgid "The average energy dissipation rate for case 2 is"
msgstr "La tasa media de disipación de energía para el caso 2 es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:79
msgid ""
"\\bar \\varepsilon_2 = \\frac{P_1}{4m_1} = \\frac{\\bar \\varepsilon_1}{4}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:81
msgid ""
"This makes sense because we are putting in the same amount of energy into a "
"control volume that is 4 times bigger."
msgstr ""
"Esto tiene sentido porque estamos invirtiendo la misma cantidad de energía "
"en un volumen de control que es 4 veces mayor."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:83
msgid "Now we calculate the velocity gradients. As previously determined,"
msgstr "Ahora calculamos los gradientes de velocidad. Como se determinó previamente,"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:85
msgid ""
"\\bar G_1 = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\bar\\varepsilon_1}{\\nu}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:87
msgid ""
"The average velocity gradient in the second control volume is simply the "
"volume weighted average"
msgstr ""
"El gradiente medio de velocidad en el segundo volumen de control es "
"simplemente el promedio ponderado por volumen"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:89
msgid ""
"\\bar G_2 = \\bar G_1\\frac{1}{4}+ 0 \\frac{3}{4}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:91
msgid ""
"where 1/4 of the case 2 control volume has the same velocity gradient as the"
" case 1 control volume and 3/4 of the control volume has a velocity gradient"
" of 0. The Camp Stein method would suggest that :math:`\\bar G_2` is equal "
"to"
msgstr ""
"donde 1/4 del volumen de control en el caso 2 tiene el mismo gradiente de "
"velocidad que el volumen de control en el caso 1 y 3/4 del volumen de "
"control tiene un gradiente de velocidad de 0. El método de Camp Stein "
"sugeriría que :math:`\\bar G_2` es igual a"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:93
msgid ""
"\\bar G_2 \\overset{?}{=} \\sqrt{\\frac{\\bar\\varepsilon_2}{\\nu}}= "
"\\sqrt{\\frac{\\bar\\varepsilon_1}{4\\nu}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:95
msgid ""
"Now we check to see if the Camp Stein method of estimating the average "
"velocity gradient, :math:`\\bar G`, is correct."
msgstr ""
"Ahora comprobamos si el método de Camp Stein para estimar el gradiente medio"
" de velocidad, :math:`\\bar G`, es correcto."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:97
msgid ""
"\\bar G_2 = \\frac{\\bar G_1}{4} \\neq "
"\\sqrt{\\frac{\\bar\\varepsilon_1}{4\\nu}} =  \\frac{\\bar G_1}{2}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:99
msgid ""
"Given that the energy dissipation rate is proportional to the square of the "
"velocity gradient, the mean of the energy dissipation rate is **not** "
"proportional to the mean of the velocity gradient. Thus the Camp Stein "
"method of calculating the average velocity gradient is not correct except in"
" the case of uniform velocity gradient. The Camp Stein equation is "
"dimensionally correct and could be corrected by adding a dimensionless "
"constant :math:`\\Pi_{CS}` that is a function of the energy dissipation rate"
" distribution within the control volume."
msgstr ""
"Dado que la tasa de disipación de energía es proporcional al cuadrado del "
"gradiente de velocidad, la media de la tasa de disipación de energía **no** "
"es proporcional a la media del gradiente de velocidad. Así, el método de "
"Camp Stein para calcular el gradiente medio de velocidad no es correcto "
"salvo en el caso del gradiente uniforme de velocidad. La ecuación de Camp "
"Stein es dimensionalmente correcta y podría corregirse añadiendo una "
"constante adimensional :math:`\\Pi_{CS}` que es función de la distribución "
"de la tasa de disipación de energía dentro del volumen de control."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:101
msgid ""
"\\bar G =\\Pi_{CS}\\sqrt{\\frac{\\bar\\varepsilon}{\\nu}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:103
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\Pi_{CS}` is 1 for a uniform velocity gradient and is less "
"than one for non uniform velocity gradients. We can think :math:`\\Pi_{CS}` "
"as a measure of the efficiency of using energy to deform the fluid. We can "
"calculate :math:`\\Pi_{CS}` for cases where we have either a Navier Stokes "
"or a computation fluid dynamics estimate of :math:`\\bar G`."
msgstr ""
"donde :math:`\\Pi_{CS}` es 1 para un gradiente de velocidad uniforme y es "
"menor que uno para gradientes de velocidad no uniformes. Podemos pensar en "
":math:`\\Pi_{CS}` como una medida de la eficiencia de usar energía para "
"deformar el fluido. Podemos calcular :math:`\\Pi_{CS}` para casos en los que"
" tenemos una estimación de Navier Stokes o una estimación computada de "
"dinámica de fluidos de :math:`\\bar G`."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:105
msgid ""
"The conventional approach to design of flocculators uses the Camp Stein "
"definition of"
msgstr ""
"El enfoque convencional para el diseño de floculadores utiliza la definición"
" de Camp Stein de"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:107
msgid "\\tilde{G} = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\bar\\varepsilon}{\\nu}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:112
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\tilde{G}` is **not** the average velocity gradient, but is "
"larger than the average velocity gradient by a factor of :math:`\\Pi_{CS}`. "
"Thus we have"
msgstr ""
"donde :math:`\\tilde{G}` **no** es el gradiente medio de velocidad, pero es "
"mayor que el gradiente medio por un factor de :math:`\\Pi_{CS}`. Así, "
"tenemos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:114
msgid "\\tilde{G} = \\Pi_{CS}\\bar G"
msgstr "\\tilde{G} = \\Pi_{CS}\\bar G"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:119
msgid ""
"Use of the Camp Stein velocity gradient in design of mixing units and "
"flocculators results in an error when applying results from one reactor to "
"another. If the energy dissipation rate distribution within the reactors is "
"different, then :math:`\\Pi_{CS}` will be different for the two reactors and"
" the actual average velocity gradient, :math:`\\bar G` will be different for"
" the two reactors."
msgstr ""
"El uso del gradiente de velocidad de Camp Stein en el diseño de unidades de "
"mezcla y floculadores provoca un error al aplicar resultados de un reactor a"
" otro. Si la distribución de la tasa de disipación de energía dentro de los "
"reactores es diferente, entonces :math:`\\Pi_{CS}` será diferente para ambos"
" reactores y el gradiente medio de velocidad real, :math:`\\bar G` será "
"diferente para ambos reactores."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:121
msgid ""
"Given that energy is used more efficiently to produce velocity gradients if "
"the velocity gradients are uniform, our goal is to design mixing and "
"flocculation units that have relatively uniform velocity gradients. If all "
"of our reactors at both research scale and municipal scale have similar "
"values of :math:`\\Pi_{CS}`, then we can use the Camp Stein definition of "
":math:`\\tilde{G}` and not introduce any significant errors. It will not be "
"reasonable, however, to expect similar performance based on similar values "
"of :math:`\\tilde{G}` if one reactor has relatively uniform energy "
"dissipation rates and the other reactor has zones with very high energy "
"dissipation rates and zones with very low energy dissipation rates."
msgstr ""
"Dado que la energía se utiliza de forma más eficiente para producir "
"gradientes de velocidad si estos son uniformes, nuestro objetivo es diseñar "
"unidades de mezcla y floculación que tengan gradientes de velocidad "
"relativamente uniformes. Si todos nuestros reactores tanto a escala de "
"investigación como a escala municipal tienen valores similares de "
":math:`\\Pi_{CS}`, entonces podemos usar la definición de :math:`\\tilde{G}`"
" de Camp Stein y no introducir errores significativos. Sin embargo, no será "
"razonable esperar un rendimiento similar basado en valores similares de "
":math:`\\tilde{G}` si un reactor tiene tasas de disipación de energía "
"relativamente uniformes y el otro tiene zonas con tasas de disipación de "
"energía muy altas y zonas con tasas de disipación energética muy bajas."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:123
msgid ""
"We will demonstrate later that mechanically mixed reactors typically have a "
"much wider range of energy dissipation rates than do well designed "
"hydraulically mixed reactors. Thus comparisons between mechanically mixed "
"and hydraulically mixed reactors must account for differences in "
":math:`\\Pi_{CS}`."
msgstr ""
"Más adelante demostraremos que los reactores mezclados mecánicamente suelen "
"tener un rango mucho más amplio de tasas de disipación de energía que los "
"reactores bien diseñados y mezclados hidráulicamente. Por tanto, las "
"comparaciones entre reactores mezclados mecánicamente y mezclados "
"hidráulicamente deben tener en cuenta las diferencias en :math:`\\Pi_{CS}`."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:125
msgid ""
"We will use the Camp Stein definition :math:`\\tilde{G} = "
"\\sqrt{\\frac{\\bar\\varepsilon}{\\nu}}` as the design parameter of "
"convenience in this textbook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:131
msgid "Estimates of Time Required for Mixing Processes"
msgstr "Estimaciones del tiempo necesario para los procesos de mezcla"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:136
msgid "Turbulent Large Scale Eddies"
msgstr "Remolinos turbulentos a gran escala"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:138
msgid ""
"The first step in mixing is at the scale of the largest eddies. The largest "
"eddies are limited in size by the smallest dimension normal to the direction"
" of flow. Thus in a pipe the dimension of the largest eddies is set by the "
"pipe diameter. In a open channel the dimension of the largest eddies is "
"usually the water depth although it could be the width of the channel for "
"the case of a narrow, deep channel."
msgstr ""
"El primer paso en la mezcla es a escala de los remuíños más grandes. Los "
"revoltijos más grandes están limitados en tamaño por la dimensión más "
"pequeña normal a la dirección del flujo. Así, en una tubería la dimensión de"
" los remolinos más grandes está determinada por el diámetro de la tubería. "
"En un canal abierto, la dimensión de los remulos más grandes suele ser la "
"profundidad del agua, aunque podría ser el ancho del canal en el caso de un "
"canal estrecho y profundo."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:140
msgid ""
"Eddy turnover time, :math:`t_{eddy}`, is the time it takes for the eddy to "
"travel a distance equal to its length-scale. Thus the eddy turnover time "
"provides a good estimate of the time required for mixing to occur at the "
"length scale of the eddy. We assume that the energy of the large eddy is "
"dissipated into smaller length scales in the time :math:`t_{eddy}`:"
msgstr ""
"El tiempo de recambio del remolino, :math:`t_{eddy}`, es el tiempo que tarda"
" el remolino en recorrer una distancia igual a su escala de longitud. Así, "
"el tiempo de recambio del remojín proporciona una buena estimación del "
"tiempo necesario para que ocurra la mezcla en la escala de longitud del "
"remolino. Asumimos que la energía del remolino grande se disipa en escalas "
"de longitud más pequeñas en el tiempo :math:`t_{eddy}`:"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:142
msgid ""
"t_{eddy} \\approx \\frac{L_{eddy}}{v_{eddy}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:144
msgid "The rate of energy loss to smaller scales is"
msgstr "La tasa de pérdida de energía a escalas más pequeñas es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:146
msgid ""
"\\bar\\varepsilon \\approx\\frac{v_{eddy}^2}{t_{eddy}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:148
msgid "Combining the two equations"
msgstr "Combinando las dos ecuaciones"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:150
msgid ""
"\\bar\\varepsilon \\approx\\frac{v_{eddy}^3}{L_{eddy}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:152
msgid ""
"We can use this equation to estimate the eddy velocity given an energy "
"dissipation rate."
msgstr ""
"Podemos usar esta ecuación para estimar la velocidad de remolí dada una tasa"
" de disipación de energía."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:154
msgid ""
"v_{eddy} \\approx \\left( \\bar\\varepsilon \\, L_{eddy} "
"\\right)^\\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:156
msgid ""
"Now we can solve for the eddy turnover time which is a measure of the mixing"
" time at the eddy scale."
msgstr ""
"Ahora podemos resolver el tiempo de recambio del relámpago, que es una "
"medida del tiempo de mezcla en la escala del remolino."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:158
msgid ""
"t_{eddy} \\approx \\frac{L_{eddy}}{\\left( \\bar\\varepsilon \\, L_{eddy} "
"\\right)^\\frac{1}{3}} \\approx \\left( \\frac{L_{eddy}^2}{ "
"\\bar\\varepsilon }\\right)^\\frac{1}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:162
msgid ""
"This provides a simple insight that the time required for an eddy to turn "
"over scales with the size of the eddy raised to the 2/3 power. Thus large "
"eddies take more time to turn over than do small eddies. Thus if we "
"calculate the time required for large scale mixing using the dimension of "
"the eddies, it will provide a reasonable estimate of the total time for "
"mixing because mixing at all smaller scales requires much less time. A "
"notable exception to this is the case of mixing in rivers. Rivers are "
"usually shallow and wide. The largest eddies in a river are limited by the "
"depth of the river. Mixing over the width of the river takes much longer "
"than vertical mixing because multiple eddies are required to transport a "
"substance from one side of the river to the other."
msgstr ""
"Esto proporciona una visión sencilla de que el tiempo necesario para que un "
"remuvicho gire escala con el tamaño del remolino elevado a la potencia de "
"2/3. Así, los remulos grandes tardan más en girar que los remolinos "
"pequeños. Por tanto, si calculamos el tiempo requerido para la mezcla a gran"
" escala usando la dimensión de los remueles, se proporcionará una estimación"
" razonable del tiempo total de mezcla, ya que mezclar a todas las escalas "
"pequeñas requiere mucho menos tiempo. Una excepción notable es el caso de la"
" mezcla en ríos. Los ríos suelen ser poco profundos y anchos. Los remolinos "
"más grandes de un río están limitados por la profundidad del río. Mezclar a "
"lo largo del ancho del río lleva mucho más tiempo que la mezcla vertical "
"porque se requieren múltiples remolinos para transportar una sustancia de un"
" lado al otro del río."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:164
msgid ""
"We can use the eddy velocity to estimate how long it will take for an eddy "
"to cross the smallest dimension of flow. Eddy velocity is :math:`v_{eddy} "
"\\approx \\left( \\bar\\varepsilon \\, L_{eddy} \\right)^\\frac{1}{3}`. The "
"“:math:`\\approx`” indicates that this relationship is the same order of "
"magnitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:167
msgid ""
"Chemical injection into the center of a pipe is common in drinking water "
"treatment plants. We can develop equations to estimate the distance required"
" for full mixing with the fluid in the pipe. In a pipe we have"
msgstr ""
"La inyección química en el centro de una tubería es común en plantas de "
"tratamiento de agua bebedor. Podemos desarrollar ecuaciones para estimar la "
"distancia necesaria para la mezcla completa con el fluido en la tubería. En "
"una tubería tenemos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:169
msgid ""
"v_{eddy} \\approx \\left( \\bar\\varepsilon \\, D \\right)^\\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:171
msgid ""
"For a long straight pipe :math:`\\bar\\varepsilon = \\frac{{\\rm f}}{2} "
"\\frac{\\bar v^3}{D}` (Equation :eq:`eq_EDR_HL`) and thus we can obtain the "
"ratio between mean velocity and the velocity of the large scale eddies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:174
msgid ""
"v_{eddy} \\approx \\left( \\frac{{\\rm f}}{2} \\frac{\\bar v^3}{D} \\, D "
"\\right)^\\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:176
msgid ""
"\\frac{v_{eddy}}{\\bar v} \\approx \\left( \\frac{{\\rm f}}{2}  "
"\\right)^\\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:178
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Given a friction factor of 0.02, the eddy velocity is approximately 20% of "
"the mean velocity. We can use this ratio to estimate how many pipe diameters"
" downstream from an injection point will the coagulant be mixed across the "
"diameter of the pipe."
msgstr ""
"Dado un factor de fricción de 0,02, la velocidad de remotos es "
"aproximadamente el 20% de la velocidad media. Podemos usar esta relación "
"para estimar cuántos diámetros de tubería aguas abajo de un punto de "
"inyección se mezclará el coagulante a lo largo del diámetro de la tubería."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:180
msgid ""
"N_{D_{pipe}} \\approx \\frac{\\bar v}{v_{eddy}} \\approx "
"\\left(\\frac{2}{{\\rm f}} \\right)^\\frac{1}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:185
msgid ""
"Where :math:`N_{D_{pipe}}` is the distance in number of pipe diameters "
"downstream of the injection point where complete mixing will have occurred. "
"This estimate is a minimum distance and a factor of safety of 2 or more "
"would reasonably be applied. In addition it is best practice to inject the "
"coagulant in the center of the pipe. Injecting the coagulant at the side of "
"the pipe will require considerably greater distance downstream for mixing "
"across the pipe."
msgstr ""
"Donde :math:`N_{D_{pipe}}` es la distancia en número de diámetros de tubería"
" aguas abajo del punto de inyección donde se habrá producido la mezcla "
"completa. Esta estimación es una distancia mínima y razonablemente se "
"aplicaría un factor de seguridad de 2 o más. Además, es buena práctica "
"inyectar el coagulante en el centro del tubo. Inyectar el coagulante en el "
"lateral del tubo requerirá una distancia considerablemente mayor aguas abajo"
" para mezclar a través del tubo."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:190
msgid "Inner Viscous Length Scale"
msgstr "Escala de longitud viscosa interna"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:192
msgid ""
"The smallest scale at which inertia containing eddies causes mixing is set "
"by the final damping of inertia by viscosity. Turbulence occurs when fluid "
"inertia is too large to be damped by viscosity. The ratio of inertia to "
"viscosity is given by the Reynolds number, :math:`\\rm Re`:"
msgstr ""
"La escala más pequeña en la que los remolinos que contienen inercia causa "
"mezcla se determina por el amortiguamiento final de la inercia por "
"viscosidad. La turbulencia ocurre cuando la inercia del fluido es demasiado "
"grande para ser amortiguada por la viscosidad. La relación de inercia a "
"viscosidad está dada por el número de Reynolds, :math:`\\rm Re`:"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:194
msgid ""
"{\\rm{Re}} = \\frac{\\bar vD}{\\nu}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:196
msgid ""
"Flows with high Reynolds numbers are turbulent (inertia dominated) and with "
"low Reynolds are laminar (viscosity dominated). The transition Reynolds "
"number is a function of the flow geometry and the velocity and length scale "
"that are used to characterize the flow. In all turbulent flows there is a "
"length scale at which inertia finally loses to viscosity. The scale where "
"viscosity wins is some multiple of the Kolmogorov length scale, which is "
"defined as:"
msgstr ""
"Los flujos con números de Reynolds altos son turbulentos (dominados por "
"inercia) y con bajos Reynolds son laminares (dominados por viscosidad). El "
"número de Reynolds de transición es función de la geometría del flujo y de "
"la escala de velocidad y longitud que se utilizan para caracterizar el "
"flujo. En todos los flujos turbulentos existe una escala de longitud en la "
"que la inercia finalmente pierde frente a la viscosidad. La escala en la que"
" prevalece la viscosidad es un múltiplo de la escala de longitud de "
"Kolmogorov, que se define como:"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:198
msgid ""
"\\eta_K = \\left( \\frac{\\nu^3}{\\varepsilon} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{4}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:200
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\eta_K` is the Kolmogorov length scale. At the Kolmogorov "
"length scale viscosity completely dampens the inertia of the eddies and "
"effectively “kills” the turbulence."
msgstr ""
"donde :math:`\\eta_K` es la escala de longitud de Kolmogorov. En la escala "
"de longitud de Kolmogorov, la viscosidad amortigua completamente la inercia "
"de los remolinos y efectivamente \"mata\" la turbulencia."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:202
msgid ""
"The length scale at which most of the kinetic energy contained in the small "
"eddies is dissipated by viscosity is the inner viscous length scale, "
":math:`\\lambda_v`, which according to Dimotakis (2000) is about `50 times "
"larger than <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0022112099007946>`_ Thus we have"
msgstr ""
"La escala de longitud en la que la mayor parte de la energía cinética "
"contenida en los pequeños remolinos se disipa por la viscosidad es la escala"
" de longitud viscosa interna, :math:`\\lambda_v`, que según Dimotakis (2000)"
" es aproximadamente `50 veces mayor que "
"<https://doi.org/10.1017/S0022112099007946>`_ Así, tenemos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:205
msgid ""
"\\lambda_\\nu = \\Pi_{K\\nu}\\left( \\frac{\\nu^3}{\\varepsilon} "
"\\right)^{\\frac{1}{4}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:210
msgid "where :math:`\\Pi_{K\\nu} = 50`"
msgstr "¿dónde :math:`\\Pi_{K\\nu} = 50`"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:212
msgid ""
"At length scales larger than the inner viscous length scale, "
":math:`\\lambda_v`, the dominant transport mechanism is by turbulent eddies."
" At length scales smaller than :math:`\\lambda_v` the dominant transport "
"mechanism is fluid deformation due to shear. If the flow regime is "
"completely laminar such as in a small diameter tube flocculator, then the "
"dominant transport mechanism is fluid deformation due to shear at length "
"scales all the way up to the diameter of the tubing."
msgstr ""
"En escalas de longitud mayores que la escala interior viscosa, "
":math:`\\lambda_v`, el mecanismo de transporte dominante es por remolinos "
"turbulentos. En escalas de longitud menores que :math:`\\lambda_v` el "
"mecanismo de transporte dominante es la deformación de fluidos debida al "
"corte. Si el régimen de flujo es completamente laminar, como en un "
"floculador tubular de pequeño diámetro, entonces el mecanismo de transporte "
"dominante es la deformación del fluido debida al cizallamiento en escalas de"
" longitud hasta el diámetro del tubo."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:214
msgid ""
"The dividing line between eddy transport and fluid deformation controlled by"
" viscosity can be calculated as a function of the energy dissipation rate "
"using :eq:`eq_inner_viscous_length`."
msgstr ""
"La línea divisoria entre el transporte de remojas y la deformación del "
"fluido controlada por la viscosidad puede calcularse en función de la tasa "
"de disipación de energía usando :eq:`eq_inner_viscous_length`."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:216
msgid ""
"`Colab worksheet for inner viscous length vs energy dissipation rate "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1N7ysHjzSBd9H4ssIT9UHRYy3pJkwu5s3#scrollTo=oizJutoQXBnU&line=5&uniqifier=1>`_"
msgstr ""
"`hoja de trabajo de Colab para longitud viscosa interior frente a tasa de "
"disipación de energía "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1N7ysHjzSBd9H4ssIT9UHRYy3pJkwu5s3#scrollTo=oizJutoQXBnU&line=5&uniqifier=1>`_"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:225
msgid "Inner viscous vs EDR"
msgstr "Viscoso interior vs EDR"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:225
msgid ""
"Eddies can cause fluid mixing down to the scale of a few millimeters for "
"energy dissipation rates used in rapid mix units and flocculators."
msgstr ""
"Los remolinos pueden provocar mezclas de fluidos a escala de unos pocos "
"milímetros para las tasas de disipación de energía utilizadas en unidades "
"mezcla rápida y floculadores."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:230
msgid "Turbulent Mixing Time as a Function of Scale"
msgstr "Tiempo de mezcla turbulento en función de la escala"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:232
msgid ""
"We are searching for the rate limiting step in the mixing process as we "
"transition from the scale of the flow down to the scale of the coagulant "
"nanoparticles. We can estimate the time required for eddies to mix at their "
"length scales by assuming that the eddies pass all of their energy to "
"smaller scales in the time it takes for an eddy to travel the distance equal"
" to the length scale of the eddy. This time is known as the `eddy turnover "
"time "
"<http://ceeserver.cee.cornell.edu/eac20/cee637/handouts/TURBFLOW_1.pdf>`__, "
":math:`t_{eddy}`. :ref:`The derivation for the equation below is found here "
"<heading_Estimates_of_time_required_for_mixing_processes>`."
msgstr ""
"Estamos buscando el paso limitante de velocidad en el proceso de mezcla "
"mientras pasamos de la escala del flujo a la escala de las nanopartículas "
"coagulantes. Podemos estimar el tiempo necesario para que los remuíños se "
"mezclen a sus escalas de longitud asumiendo que los remolinos pasan toda su "
"energía a escalas más pequeñas en el tiempo que tarda un remolino en "
"recorrer la distancia igual a la escala de longitud del remolino. Este "
"tiempo se conoce como el tiempo de recambio del remolino "
"`<http://ceeserver.cee.cornell.edu/eac20/cee637/handouts/TURBFLOW_1.pdf>`__,"
" :math:`t_{eddy}`. :ref:`The derivation for the equation below is found here"
" <heading_Estimates_of_time_required_for_mixing_processes>`."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:235
msgid ""
" t_{eddy} \\approx \\left( \\frac{L_{eddy}^2}{ \\bar\\varepsilon "
"}\\right)^\\frac{1}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:240
msgid ""
"We can plot the eddy turnover time as a function of scale from the inner "
"viscous length scale up to the scale of the flow. We will discover whether "
"large scale mixing by eddies is faster or slower than small scale mixing by "
"eddies."
msgstr ""
"Podemos graficar el tiempo de recambio de remoles en función de la escala "
"desde la escala interior de longitud viscosa hasta la escala del flujo. "
"Descubriremos si la mezcla a gran escala por remolinos es más rápida o más "
"lenta que la mezcla a pequeña escala por remolinos."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:242
msgid ""
"`Colab worksheet calculating the eddy turnover time "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1N7ysHjzSBd9H4ssIT9UHRYy3pJkwu5s3#scrollTo=4zUMlZy8bR1Z>`_"
msgstr ""
"`hoja de trabajo de Colab calculando el tiempo de relevo de relámpago "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1N7ysHjzSBd9H4ssIT9UHRYy3pJkwu5s3#scrollTo=4zUMlZy8bR1Z>`_"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:251
msgid "Eddy turnover time"
msgstr "Tiempo de cambio de relámpago"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:251
msgid ""
"Small eddies turn in less time than large eddies. This is why the mixing at "
"the largest scale dominates the mixing time."
msgstr ""
"Los remolinos pequeños se producen en menos tiempo que los remolinos "
"grandes. Por eso la mezcla a mayor escala domina el tiempo de mezcla."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:257
msgid "Shear-Diffusion Transport"
msgstr "Transporte por cizalladura y difusión"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:259
msgid ""
"After the first few seconds in which mixing occurs from the length scale of "
"the flow down to the inner viscous length scale the next step in the "
"transport process is blending of the coagulant uniformly with the raw water."
" At the end of the turbulent transport the coagulant stock has been "
"stretched out into thin bands throughout the raw water, but the two fluids "
"are not actually blended together by turbulence. The blending is "
"accomplished by a combination of fluid deformation controlled by viscous "
"shear and then by molecular diffusion."
msgstr ""
"Tras los primeros segundos en los que se produce la mezcla desde la escala "
"de longitud del flujo hasta la escala interior viscosa, el siguiente paso en"
" el proceso de transporte es la mezcla uniforme del coagulante con el agua "
"cruda. Al final del transporte turbulento, el material coagulante se ha "
"extendido en bandas delgadas a lo largo del agua cruda, pero los dos fluidos"
" no se mezclan realmente por la turbulencia. La mezcla se logra mediante una"
" combinación de deformación del fluido controlada por cizalladura viscosa y "
"luego por difusión molecular."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:264
msgid "Fluid Deformation by Shear"
msgstr "Deformación del fluido por cizalladura"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:266
msgid ""
"The time scale for fluid deformation is :math:`1/G` where :math:`G` is the "
"velocity gradient. This simple relationship is because the velocity of fluid"
" deformation is proportional to the length scale and thus the time to travel"
" any given distance in a linear velocity gradient is always the same. "
"Velocity gradients in conventional mechanized rapid mix units are order 1000"
" Hz and thus the time for fluid deformation to blur concentration gradients "
"is approximately 1 ms. This confirms the idea that blending the coagulant "
"with the raw water is actually a very fast process with the slowest phase "
"being the transport by turbulent eddies at the scale of reactor."
msgstr ""
"La escala temporal para la deformación del fluido es :math:`1/G` donde "
":math:`G` es el gradiente de velocidad. Esta relación simple se debe a que "
"la velocidad de deformación del fluido es proporcional a la escala de "
"longitud y, por tanto, el tiempo para recorrer cualquier distancia dada en "
"un gradiente lineal de velocidad es siempre el mismo. Los gradientes de "
"velocidad en unidades mezcla rápida mecanizadas convencionales son del orden"
" de 1000 Hz y, por tanto, el tiempo para que la deformación del fluido "
"difumine los gradientes de concentración es aproximadamente 1 ms. Esto "
"confirma la idea de que mezclar el coagulante con el agua cruda es en "
"realidad un proceso muy rápido, siendo la fase más lenta el transporte por "
"remoles turbulentos a escala de reactor."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:268
msgid ""
"The full time required for fluid deformation to achieve blending down to the"
" scale where molecular diffusion takes over is likely a multiple of 1/G "
"where the multiple is determined by the number of different directions that "
"the fluid must be sheared in to reach close to uniform blending. However, "
"even multiplying 1/G by a factor of 10 still results in very rapid mixing."
msgstr ""
"El tiempo completo necesario para que la deformación del fluido logre la "
"mezcla hasta la escala en la que la difusión molecular toma el control "
"probablemente sea un múltiplo de 1/G, donde el múltiplo está determinado por"
" el número de direcciones diferentes en las que el fluido debe ser cortado "
"para alcanzar una mezcla casi uniforme. Sin embargo, incluso multiplicar 1/G"
" por un factor de 10 sigue resultando en una mezcla muy rápida."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:273
msgid "Einstein’s Diffusion Equation"
msgstr "La ecuación de difusión de Einstein"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:275
msgid ""
"The final step of mixing is mediated by molecular diffusion. We can estimate"
" the length scale at which fluid shear and diffusion provide transport at "
"the same rate. Einstein’s diffusion equation is"
msgstr ""
"El paso final de mezcla está mediado por la difusión molecular. Podemos "
"estimar la escala de longitud en la que el cizallamiento y la difusión del "
"fluido proporcionan transporte a la misma velocidad. La ecuación de difusión"
" de Einstein es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:277
msgid "D_{Diffusion} = \\frac{k_B T}{3 \\pi \\mu D_P}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:282
msgid ""
"where :math:`k_B` is the Boltzmann constant and :math:`d_P` is the diameter "
"of the particle that is diffusion in a fluid with viscosity :math:`\\nu` and"
" density :math:`\\rho`. The diffusion coefficient :math:`D_{Diffusion}` has "
"dimensions of :math:`\\frac{[L^2]}{[T]}` and can be understood as the "
"velocity of the particle multiplied by the length of the mean free path. "
"From dimensional analysis the time for diffusion to blur a concentration "
"gradient over a length scale, :math:`L_{Diffusion}` is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:284
msgid ""
"t_{Diffusion} \\approx \\frac{L_{Diffusion}^2}{D_{Diffusion}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:286
msgid ""
"The shear time scale is :math:`1/G` and thus we can solve for the length "
"scale at which diffusion and shear have equivalent transport rates."
msgstr ""
"La escala de tiempo de cizallamiento es :math:`1/G` y por tanto podemos "
"resolver la escala de longitud en la que la difusión y el cizallamiento "
"tienen tasas de transporte equivalentes."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:288
msgid ""
