#, python-format
msgid ""
"Coiled tubes are used as flocculators at laboratory scale. The one shown "
"below is a doubled coil. A single coil would only go around one cylinder. "
"The `double coiled tube flocculators were used extensively by the AguaClara "
"team at Cornell University <https://github.com/AguaClara/Research-"
"Archive/blob/main/2014%20Spring%20Laminar%20Tube%20Flocculator.pdf>`__."
msgstr ""
"Los tubos en espiral se utilizan como floculadores a escala de laboratorio. "
"El que se muestra a continuación es una bobina doble. Una bobina simple solo"
" daría la vuelta a un cilindro. Los floculadores de tubos dobles de `bobinas"
" fueron utilizados extensamente por el equipo de AguaClara en la Universidad"
" de Cornell <https://github.com/AguaClara/Research-"
"Archive/blob/main/2014%20Spring%20Laminar%20Tube%20Flocculator.pdf>`__."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:603
msgid "double coiled tube flocculator"
msgstr "Floculador de tubo doble bobinado"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:603
msgid ""
"The double coiled laminar flow flocculator creates secondary currents that "
"oscillate in direction. This may be helpful in creating much more mixing "
"than would occur in a straight laminar flow pipe."
msgstr ""
"El floculador de doble bobina laminar de flujo crea corrientes secundarias "
"que oscilan en dirección. Esto puede ser útil para crear mucha más mezcla de"
" lo que ocurriría en un tubo de flujo laminar recto."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:605
msgid ""
"The ratio of the coiled to straight friction factors is given by `Mishra and"
" Gupta <https://doi.org/10.1021/i260069a017>`__. The Dean number is defined "
"as:"
msgstr ""
"La relación entre los factores de fricción enrollados y rectos está dada por"
" `Mishra y Gupta <https://doi.org/10.1021/i260069a017>`__. El número de Dean"
" se define como:"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:607
msgid "De = Re\\left(\\frac{D}{D_c}\\right)^\\frac{1}{2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:611
msgid ""
"where :math:`D` is the inner diameter of the tube and :math:`D_c` is the "
"diameter of the coil. Note that the tubing coils are actually helices and "
"that for the tubing diameters and coil diameters used for flocculators that "
"the helix doesn’t significantly change the radius of curvature."
msgstr ""
"donde :math:`D` es el diámetro interior del tubo y :math:`D_c` es el "
"diámetro de la bobina. Ten en cuenta que las bobinas de la tubería son en "
"realidad hélices y que para los diámetros de las tuberías y las bobinas "
"usadas para floculadores, la hélice no cambia significativamente el radio de"
" curvatura."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:613
msgid "\\frac{{\\rm f}_{coil}}{{\\rm f}} = 1 + 0.033\\left(log_{10}De\\right)^4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:617
msgid ""
"h_{L_{coil}} = h_{{\\rm f}} \\left[ 1 + 0.033\\left(log_{10}De\\right)^4 "
"\\right]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:621
msgid ""
"where :math:`h_{{\\rm f}} = \\frac{32\\nu L\\bar v}{ g D^2}`. Note that we "
"switch from major losses to total head loss here because the head loss from "
"flowing around the coil is no longer simply due to shear on the wall."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:624
msgid ""
"h_{L_{coil}} = \\frac{32\\nu L\\bar v}{ g D^2} \\left[ 1 + "
"0.033\\left(log_{10}De\\right)^4 \\right]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:630
msgid ""
"\\bar\\varepsilon = 32\\nu \\left( \\frac{\\bar v}{D} \\right)^2 \\left[ 1 +"
" 0.033\\left(log_{10}De\\right)^4 \\right]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:634
msgid ""
"The average velocity gradient is proportional to the square root of the head"
" loss and thus we obtain"
msgstr ""
"El gradiente medio de velocidad es proporcional a la raíz cuadrada del "
"pérdida de carga y así obtenemos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:636
msgid ""
"G_{CS_{coil}} = \\tilde{G}\\left[ 1 + 0.033\\left(log_{10}De\\right)^4  "
"\\right]^\\frac{1}{2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:640
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\tilde{G} =4\\sqrt2 \\frac{\\bar v}{D}` for laminar flow in a "
"straight pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:642
msgid ""
"G_{CS_{coil}} = 4\\sqrt2 \\frac{\\bar v}{D}\\left[ 1 + "
"0.033\\left(log_{10}De\\right)^4  \\right]^\\frac{1}{2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:650
msgid "Flow in Porous Media"
msgstr "Flujo en medios porosos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:652
msgid ""
"The `Ergun equation <https://neutrium.net/fluid_flow/pressure-drop-through-a"
"-packed-bed/>`_ applies to both laminar and turbulent flow through packed "
"beds."
msgstr ""
"La ecuación de `Ergun <https://neutrium.net/fluid_flow/pressure-drop-"
"through-a-packed-bed/>`_ se aplica tanto al flujo laminar como al turbulento"
" a través de lechos compactados."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:654
msgid ""
"  h_f = \\frac{L}{2g D_{sand}} \\left( 300 \\frac{\\nu v_a "
"(1-\\phi)^2}{D_{sand} \\phi^3} + 3.5 \\frac{v_a^2 (1-\\phi) }{\\phi^3} "
"\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:659
msgid ""
"The Ergun equation can be rewritten to be consistent with the format of the "
"Darcy-Weisbach equation. To do this we add a factor of 2 to the definition "
"of the Ergun friction factor and will divide by the factor of 2 in a "
"subsequent equation. The modified Ergun friction factor is"
msgstr ""
"La ecuación de Ergun puede reescribirse para ser consistente con el formato "
"de la ecuación de Darcy-Weisbach. Para ello añadimos un factor de 2 a la "
"definición del factor de fricción de Ergun y dividiremos por el factor de 2 "
"en una ecuación posterior. El factor de fricción de Ergun modificado es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:661
msgid "  f_{\\phi} = \\frac{300}{Re_{\\phi}} + 3.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:666
msgid ""
"where the :math:`Re_{\\phi}` includes the porosity effect on the velocity "
"and is given by"
msgstr ""
"donde el :math:`Re_{\\phi}` incluye el efecto de porosidad sobre la "
"velocidad y está dado por"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:668
msgid "  Re_{\\phi} = \\frac{v_a D_{sand}}{\\nu(1-\\phi)}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:673
msgid ""
"I added a factor of two into the denominator to be consistent with the "
"Darcy-Weisbach equation to obtain the modified Ergun equation."
msgstr ""
"Sumé un factor de dos al denominador para que fuera consistente con la "
"ecuación de Darcy-Weisbach y así obtener la ecuación de Ergun modificada."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:675
msgid ""
"  h_f = f_{\\phi} \\frac{L}{D_{sand}} \\frac{v_a^2}{2g} "
"\\frac{(1-\\phi)}{\\phi^3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:680
msgid "The residence time in a porous media bed is given by"
msgstr "El tiempo de residencia en una cama porosa de medios se da por"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:682
msgid "\\theta = \\frac{L\\phi} {v_a}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:686
msgid "Now we can calculate the average energy dissipation rate in porous media."
msgstr ""
"Ahora podemos calcular la tasa media de disipación de energía en medios "
"porosos."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:688
msgid "\\bar\\varepsilon = \\frac{g h_f}{\\theta}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:692
msgid "Substituting the equations for head loss and residence times we obtain"
msgstr ""
"Sustituyendo las ecuaciones por tiempos de pérdida de carga y residencia "
"obtenemos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:694
msgid ""
" \\bar\\varepsilon = \\frac{f_{\\phi}}{2} \\frac{v_a^3}{D_{sand}} "
"\\frac{(1-\\phi)}{\\phi^4}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:699
msgid "The Camp Stein velocity gradient for flow in porous media is"
msgstr "El gradiente de velocidad de Camp Stein para el flujo en medios porosos es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:701
msgid ""
"  \\tilde{G} = \\left(\\frac{f_{\\phi}}{2\\nu} \\frac{v_a^3}{D_{sand}} "
"\\frac{(1-\\phi)}{\\phi^4}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:710
#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:852
msgid "Expansions"
msgstr "Expansiones"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:712
msgid ""
"The average energy dissipation rate for a flow expansion really only has "
"meaning if there is a defined control volume where the mechanical energy is "
"lost. Hydraulic flocculators provide such a case because the same flow "
"expansion is repeated and thus the mechanical energy loss can be assumed to "
"happen in the volume associated with one flow expansion. In this case we "
"have"
msgstr ""
"La tasa media de disipación de energía para una expansión de flujo solo "
"tiene realmente significado si existe un volumen de control definido donde "
"se pierde la energía mecánica. Los floculadores hidráulicos proporcionan "
"este caso porque se repite la misma expansión del flujo y, por tanto, se "
"puede asumir que la pérdida de energía mecánica ocurre en el volumen "
"asociado a una expansión de flujo. En este caso tenemos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:714
msgid "h_e =  K\\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2}{2g}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:718
msgid ""
"In this Equation :math:`K` represents the fraction of the kinetic energy "
"that is dissipated."
msgstr ""
"En esta ecuación, :math:`K` representa la fracción de la energía cinética "
"que se disipa."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:720
msgid ""
"If we define the length of the control volume (in the direction of flow) as "
":math:`H` then the residence time is"
msgstr ""
"Si definimos la longitud del volumen de control (en la dirección del flujo) "
"como :math:`H` entonces el tiempo de residencia es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:722
msgid "\\theta = \\frac{H}{\\bar v}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:726
msgid "\\bar\\varepsilon = \\frac{gh_{\\rm{e}}}{\\theta}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:730
msgid "Combining the previous equations we obtain"
msgstr "Combinando las ecuaciones anteriores obtenemos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:732
msgid "\\bar\\varepsilon = K\\frac{\\bar v_{out}^3}{2H}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:736
msgid ""
"The Camp Stein velocity gradient, Equation :eq:`G_Camp_Stein`, converts the "
"energy dissipation rate into a velocity gradient."
msgstr ""
"El gradiente de velocidad de Camp Stein, ecuación :eq:`G_Camp_Stein`, "
"convierte la tasa de disipación de energía en un gradiente de velocidad."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:738
msgid "\\tilde{G} = \\bar v_{out}\\sqrt{\\frac{K\\bar v_{out}}{2H\\nu}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:746
msgid "Maximum Velocity Gradients"
msgstr "Gradientes de velocidad máxima"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:751
msgid "Straight Pipe (Major Losses)"
msgstr "Tubería recta (Pérdidas Mayores)"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:753
msgid ""
"The maximum velocity gradient in pipe flow occurs at the wall. This is true "
"for both laminar and turbulent flow. In either case a force balance on a "
"control volume of pipe gives us the wall shear and the wall shear can then "
"be used to estimate the velocity gradient at the wall."
msgstr ""
"El gradiente máximo de velocidad en el flujo de tubería ocurre en la pared. "
"Esto es cierto tanto para el flujo laminar como para el turbulento. En "
"cualquier caso, un balance de fuerzas en un volumen de control de tubería "
"nos da la cizalla de pared y la cizalladura puede usarse para estimar el "
"gradiente de velocidad en la pared."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:763
#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:917
msgid "Pipe pressure and shear force balance"
msgstr "Equilibrio de presión en tubería y fuerzas cortantes"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:763
msgid ""
"A fluid flowing from left to right due to a pressure gradient results in "
"wall shear."
msgstr ""
"Un fluido que fluye de izquierda a derecha debido a un gradiente de presión "
"provoca cizalladura de pared."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:765
msgid ""
"A force balance for the case of steady flow in a round pipe requires that "
"sum of the forces in the x direction must equal zero. Given a pipe with "
"diameter, D, and length, L, we obtain"
msgstr ""
"Un balance de fuerzas para el caso de un flujo estacionario en una tubería "
"redonda requiere que la suma de las fuerzas en la dirección x sea igual a "
"cero. Dada una tubería con diámetro, D y longitud, L, obtenemos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:767
msgid "\\left(P_{in}- P_{out}\\right)\\frac{\\pi D^2}{4} = \\tau_{wall} \\pi D L"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:771
msgid "-\\Delta P\\frac{D}{4} = \\tau_{wall} L"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:775
msgid "For this control volume the energy equation simplifies to"
msgstr "Para este volumen de control, la ecuación de energía se simplifica a"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:777
msgid "-\\Delta P=\\rho g h_{{\\rm f}}"
msgstr "-\\Delta P=\\rho g h_{{\\rm f}}"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:781
msgid "The relationship between shear and velocity gradient is"
msgstr "La relación entre cizallamiento y gradiente de velocidad es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:783
msgid "\\tau_{wall} = \\mu \\frac{du}{dy}_{wall} = \\nu \\rho G_{wall}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:787
msgid ""
"Combining the energy equation, the force balance, and the relationship "
"between shear and velocity gradient we obtain"
msgstr ""
"Combinando la ecuación de energía, el balance de fuerzas y la relación entre"
" cizallamiento y gradiente de velocidad obtenemos"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:789
msgid "\\rho g h_{{\\rm f}}\\frac{D}{4} = \\nu \\rho G_{wall} L"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:793
msgid "G_{wall} = \\frac{g h_{{\\rm f}}D}{4\\nu L}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:797
msgid ""
"This equation is valid for both laminar flow. For turbulent flow it is "
"necessary to make the approximation that wall shear perpendicular to the "
"direction of flow is insignificant in increasing the magnitude of the wall "
"shear. We can substitute the Darcy Weisbach equation for head loss to obtain"
msgstr ""
"Esta ecuación es válida tanto para el flujo laminar. Para el flujo "
"turbulento es necesario hacer la aproximación de que el cizallamiento de "
"pared perpendicular a la dirección del flujo es insignificante para aumentar"
" la magnitud del cizallamiento de pared. Podemos sustituir la ecuación de "
"Darcy-Weisbach por pérdida de carga obtener"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:799
msgid "G_{wall} ={\\rm f}  \\frac{\\bar v^2}{8\\nu}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:804
#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:825
msgid "The energy dissipation rate at the wall is"
msgstr "La tasa de disipación de energía en la pared es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:806
#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:827
msgid "\\varepsilon_{wall} = G_{wall}^2 \\nu"
msgstr "\\varepsilon_{wall} = G_{wall}^2 \\nu"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:810
msgid ""
"\\varepsilon_{wall} = \\frac{1}{\\nu}\\left({\\rm f}  \\frac{\\bar v^2}{8} "
"\\right)^2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:815
msgid ""
"For laminar flow we can substitute :math:`{\\rm f} = \\frac{64}{{\\rm Re}}` "
"and the definition of the Reynolds number to obtain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:817
msgid " G_{wall} =  \\frac{8\\bar v}{D}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:823
msgid ""
"This equation is useful for finding the velocity gradient at the wall of a "
"tube settler."
msgstr ""
"Esta ecuación es útil para encontrar el gradiente de velocidad en la pared "
"de un sedimentador de tubos."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:831
msgid "\\varepsilon_{wall} = \\left(\\frac{8\\bar v}{D} \\right)^2 \\nu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:840
msgid ""
"The shear on the wall of a coiled tube is not uniform. The outside of the "
"curve has a higher velocity gradient than the inside of the curve and there "
"are secondary currents that results in wall shear that is not purely in the "
"locally defined upstream direction. We do not have a precise equation for "
"the wall shear. The best we can do currently is define an average wall shear"
" in the locally defined direction of flow by combining "
":math:`G_{{CS}_{wall_{coil}}} =\\rm{f_{coil}} \\frac{\\bar v^2}{8\\nu}` and "
":math:`{\\rm f}_{coil} = {\\rm f} \\left[ 1 + "
"0.033\\left(log_{10}De\\right)^4 \\right]` to obtain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:845
msgid ""
"G_{{CS}_{wall_{coil}}} ={\\rm f} \\left[ 1 + 0.033 \\left(log_{10}De "
"\\right)^4 \\right]  \\frac{\\bar v^2}{8\\nu}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:854
msgid ""
"Flow expansions are used intentionally or unavoidable in multiple locations "
"in hydraulically optimized water treatment plants. Rapid mix and hydraulic "
"flocculation use flow expansions to generate fluid mixing and collisions "
"between particles. Flow expansions are responsible for minor losses and the "
"rate at which expansions dissipate energy increases as the dimension of the "
"jet decreases."
msgstr ""
"Las expansiones de flujo se utilizan de forma intencionada o inevitable en "
"múltiples ubicaciones en plantas de tratamiento de agua optimizadas "
"hidráulicamente. mezcla rápida y la floculación hidráulica utilizan "
"expansiones de flujo para generar mezcla de fluidos y colisiones entre "
"partículas. Las expansiones de flujo son responsables de pérdidas menores y "
"la velocidad a la que las expansiones disipan la energía aumenta a medida "
"que disminuye la dimensión del chorro."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:859
msgid "Round Jet"
msgstr "Chorro redondo"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:861
msgid ""
"The energy dissipation rate at the centerline of a round jet is a well "
"studied phenomenon (`Baldyga, et al. 1995 "
"<https://doi.org/10.1016/0009-2509(95)00049-B>`__)."
msgstr ""
"La tasa de disipación de energía en la línea central de un chorro redondo es"
" un fenómeno bien estudiado (`Baldyga, et al. 1995 "
"<https://doi.org/10.1016/0009-2509(95)00049-B>`__)."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:864
msgid ""
"\\varepsilon_{Centerline} = \\frac{50 D_{Jet}^3 \\bar v_{Jet}^3}{ \\left( x "
"- 2 D_{Jet} \\right)^4}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:868
msgid ""
"The maximum energy dissipation rate occurs at approximately 7D downstream "
"from the origin of the jet."
msgstr ""
"La tasa máxima de disipación de energía ocurre aproximadamente a 7D aguas "
"abajo del origen del chorro."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:870
msgid ""
"\\varepsilon_{max} = \\frac{\\left( \\frac{50}{\\left( 5 \\right)^4} "
"\\right) \\bar v_{Jet}^3}{D_{Jet}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:874
msgid ""
"The measured dimensionless coefficient, :math:`\\Pi_{JetRound}`, is "
"proportional to the fraction of the kinetic energy that is dissipated in the"
" time required for the jet to travel a distance equal to its original "
"diameter. The higher this coefficient the faster the jet dissipates its "
"energy. The coefficient is only a function of the geometry of the jet and "
"thus round jets and plane jets have different coefficients."
msgstr ""
"El coeficiente adimensional medido, :math:`\\Pi_{JetRound}`, es proporcional"
" a la fracción de la energía cinética que se disipa en el tiempo que el "
"chorro recorre una distancia igual a su diámetro original. Cuanto mayor es "
"este coeficiente, más rápido disipa la energía del chorro. El coeficiente es"
" solo función de la geometría del chorro y, por tanto, los chorros redondos "
"y los chorros planos tienen coeficientes diferentes."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:876
msgid "\\varepsilon_{max} = \\Pi_{JetRound} \\frac{\\bar v_{Jet} ^3}{D_{Jet}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:881
msgid "\\Pi_{JetRound} = 0.08"
msgstr "\\Pi_{JetRound} = 0,08"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:886
msgid "The maximum velocity gradient in a round jet is thus"
msgstr "El gradiente máximo de velocidad en un chorro redondo es por tanto"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:888
msgid ""
" G_{max} = \\bar v_{Jet} \\sqrt{\\frac{\\Pi_{JetRound} \\bar v_{Jet} }{\\nu "
"D_{Jet}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:893
msgid ""
"The maximum permissible velocity gradient in a round jet given a maximum "
"allowable velocity gradient is"
msgstr ""
"El gradiente máximo de velocidad permitido en un chorro redondo dado un "
"gradiente máximo de velocidad permitido es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:895
msgid ""
"\\bar v_{Jet_{max}} = G_{max}^{\\frac{2}{3}} \\left(\\frac{\\nu "
"D_{Jet}}{\\Pi_{JetRound} }\\right)^{\\frac{1}{3}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:900
msgid ""
"The minimum jet diameter given a maximum allowable velocity gradient and "
"required jet velocity is"
msgstr ""
"El diámetro mínimo del chorro dado un gradiente máximo de velocidad "
"permitido y la velocidad del chorro requerida es"

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:902
msgid "D_{Jet_{min}}= \\frac{\\Pi_{JetRound} \\bar v_{Jet}^3}{\\nu G_{max}^2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:907
msgid ""
"Below we plot the Baldyga et al. equation for the energy dissipation rate as"
" a function of distance from the discharge location for the case of a round "
"jet that is discharging into a large tank."
msgstr ""
"A continuación representamos la ecuación de Baldyga et al. para la tasa de "
"disipación de energía en función de la distancia desde la ubicación de "
"descarga en el caso de un chorro redondo que se descarga en un tanque "
"grande."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:917
msgid ""
"The centerline energy dissipation rate downstream from a round jet. The "
"distance downstream is measured in units of jet diameters. The energy "
"dissipation rate between the jet and 7 jet diameters is developing as the "
"shear between the stationary fluid and the jet propagates toward the center "
"of the jet and turbulence is generated."
msgstr ""
"La tasa de disipación de energía en la línea central aguas abajo de un "
"chorro redondo. La distancia aguas abajo se mide en unidades de diámetros de"
" chorro. La tasa de disipación de energía entre el chorro y 7 diámetros de "
"chorro se desarrolla a medida que el corte entre el fluido estacionario y el"
" chorro se propaga hacia el centro del chorro y se genera turbulencia."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:919
msgid ""
"By substituting the continuity equation into Equation :eq:`roundjet_G_max` "
"we can find the minimum jet diameter given a maximum allowed velocity "
"gradient."
msgstr ""
"Sustituyendo la ecuación de continuidad en la ecuación :eq:`roundjet_G_max` "
"podemos encontrar el diámetro mínimo del chorro dado un gradiente máximo "
"permitido de velocidad."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:921
msgid ""
" G_{max} = \\left(\\frac{4 Q}{\\pi D_{Jet}^2}\\right)^\\frac{3}{2} "
"\\sqrt{\\frac{\\Pi_{JetRound}  }{\\nu D_{Jet}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:926
msgid ""
"Solve for :math:`D_{Jet}` to obtain the minimum jet diameter to deliver a "
"target flow without exceeding the maximum velocity gradient."
msgstr ""
"Resuelve :math:`D_{Jet}` para obtener el diámetro mínimo del chorro que "
"permita entregar un flujo objetivo sin exceder el gradiente máximo de "
"velocidad."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:928
msgid ""
" D_{Jet} = \\left[\\frac{\\Pi_{JetRound}  }{\\nu G_{max}^2}  \\left(\\frac{4"
" Q}{\\pi }\\right)^3 \\right]^\\frac{1}{7}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:933
msgid ""
"Equation :eq:`D_jet_min_of_jet_G_max` allows us to make the connection "
"between a flow contraction and the resulting maximum velocity gradient. As "
"we design flow passages where there are constraints on the maximum velocity "
"gradient we need to calculate the minimum pipe diameter. The pipe diameter "
"can be obtained by substituting Equation :eq:`D_pipe_of_D_vc`."
msgstr ""
"La ecuación :eq:`D_jet_min_of_jet_G_max` nos permite establecer la conexión "
"entre una contracción de flujo y el gradiente de velocidad máxima "
"resultante. Al diseñar pasajes de flujo donde existen restricciones sobre el"
" gradiente máximo de velocidad, necesitamos calcular el diámetro mínimo de "
"la tubería. El diámetro de la tubería se puede obtener sustituyendo por la "
"ecuación :eq:`D_pipe_of_D_vc`."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:935
msgid ""
" D_{pipe_{min}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\Pi_{vc}}} \\left[\\frac{\\Pi_{JetRound}"
"  }{\\nu G_{max}^2}  \\left(\\frac{4 Q}{\\pi }\\right)^3 "
"\\right]^\\frac{1}{7}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:940
msgid ""
"For many geometry changes we know the minor loss coefficient. An equivalent "
"equation that is a function of the minor loss coefficient can be obtained by"
" substituting Equation :eq:`pi_vc_of_minor_K` into Equation "
":eq:`D_pipe_min_of_jet_G_max`."
msgstr ""
"Para muchos cambios geométricos conocemos el coeficiente de pérdida menor. "
"Una ecuación equivalente que es función del coeficiente de pérdida menor "
"puede obtenerse sustituyendo la ecuación :eq:`pi_vc_of_minor_K` por la "
"ecuación :eq:`D_pipe_min_of_jet_G_max`."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:942
msgid ""
" D_{pipe_{min}} = \\sqrt{\\sqrt{K_e} + 1} \\left[\\frac{\\Pi_{JetRound}  "
"}{\\nu G_{max}^2}  \\left(\\frac{4 Q}{\\pi }\\right)^3 \\right]^\\frac{1}{7}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:947
msgid ""
"Equation :eq:`D_pipe_min_of_K_and_jet_G_max` is limited to geometries where "
"any flow contractions in series are sufficiently separated so that the flow "
"completely expands before entering the next contraction. The pipe diameter "
"is then set by the largest minor loss coefficient in the pipe system."
msgstr ""
"La ecuación :eq:`D_pipe_min_of_K_and_jet_G_max` se limita a geometrías donde"
" cualquier contracción de flujo en serie está suficientemente separada para "
"que el flujo se expanda completamente antes de entrar en la siguiente "
"contracción. El diámetro de la tubería se determina entonces por el mayor "
"coeficiente de pérdida menor en el sistema de tuberías."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:949
msgid ""
"The maximum flow that can be handled by a pipe with minor losses can be "
"obtained by solving Equation :eq:`D_pipe_min_of_K_and_jet_G_max` for the "
"flow rate."
msgstr ""
"El caudal máximo que puede manejar una tubería con pérdidas menores se "
"obtiene resolviendo la Ecuación :eq:`D_pipe_min_of_K_and_jet_G_max` para la "
"caudal."

#: ../../Fluid_Deformation_and_Energy_Dissipation/FDED_Derivations.rst:951
msgid ""
"Q_{max} = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\left[\\frac{\\nu G_{max}^2}{\\Pi_{JetRound}} "
"\\left(\\frac{D_{pipe}}{\\sqrt{\\sqrt{K_e} + "
"1}}\\right)^7\\right]^\\frac{1}{3}"
msgstr ""

